22. EXECUTION INSTRUCTIONS

Work in the following order:

PHASE A — Establish the design system.
Create typography, colours, spacing, components, icons, buttons and layout rules.

PHASE B — Build the complete application shell.
Create the sidebar, top navigation, page containers and routing architecture.

PHASE C — Build all major department pages.
Implement every department and its key screens.

PHASE D — Connect the user journeys.
Ensure all relevant pages, actions and workflows are navigable.

PHASE E — Add prototype interactions.
Implement forms, tabs, dialogs, tasks, mock AI workflows and state changes.

PHASE F — Review the complete product.
Inspect every route and refine inconsistencies.

IMPORTANT:

Do not stop after creating the landing page or dashboard.

Do not replace complex pages with placeholder cards.

Do not omit departments because the application is large.

Prioritise a working, complete navigation system and all major page containers before polishing minor details.

If the application is too large to implement in one generation, build it incrementally while preserving the same design system, routing architecture and shared components.

Keep a visible list of completed and remaining screens.

FINAL DELIVERABLE:

A complete, navigable, responsive, high-fidelity BrainWise SaaS frontend prototype.

The product owner must be able to log in using a demo flow, explore every department, navigate every major page, experience the entire user journey, test the principal interactions and evaluate the visual design before approving the final UI/UX.

The ultimate design objective:

BrainWise should look and feel like a premium business intelligence platform built for serious founders — minimal, intelligent, beautifully organised and exceptionally easy to use.